WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.256
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online English for Academic Purposes.

2
00:00:06.556 --> 00:00:10.151
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.451 --> 00:00:16.192
Unit eight: Essay Structure. Today you will plan and organise a short academic essay.

4
00:00:16.492 --> 00:00:19.307
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:23.558
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.417 --> 00:00:25.255
Essay.

7
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.714
Essay means a piece of writing on a topic.

8
00:00:29.317 --> 00:00:30.631
Write a short essay.

9
00:00:31.217 --> 00:00:33.416
Your turn. Say: Essay.

10
00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:36.896
Essay.

11
00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:38.814
Introduction.

12
00:00:39.817 --> 00:00:42.106
Introduction means the opening part.

13
00:00:42.717 --> 00:00:44.345
Begin with an introduction.

14
00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:47.533
Your turn. Say: Introduction.

15
00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:51.588
Introduction.

16
00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:53.223
Thesis.

17
00:00:54.217 --> 00:00:56.739
Thesis means the main argument of an essay.

18
00:00:57.350 --> 00:00:59.036
State your thesis clearly.

19
00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:01.931
Your turn. Say: Thesis.

20
00:01:04.767 --> 00:01:05.675
Thesis.

21
00:01:06.417 --> 00:01:07.186
Body.

22
00:01:08.183 --> 00:01:10.299
Body means the middle part of an essay.

23
00:01:10.883 --> 00:01:12.941
The body has three paragraphs.

24
00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:15.715
Your turn. Say: Body.

25
00:01:18.567 --> 00:01:19.336
Body.

26
00:01:20.083 --> 00:01:21.142
Conclusion.

27
00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:24.068
Conclusion means the final part.

28
00:01:24.683 --> 00:01:26.126
End with a conclusion.

29
00:01:26.717 --> 00:01:29.427
Your turn. Say: Conclusion.

30
00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:33.279
Conclusion.

31
00:01:34.017 --> 00:01:35.204
Outline.

32
00:01:36.217 --> 00:01:38.344
Outline means a plan before writing.

33
00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:40.392
Make an outline first.

34
00:01:40.983 --> 00:01:43.787
Your turn. Say: Outline.

35
00:01:46.633 --> 00:01:47.716
Outline.

36
00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:49.556
Background.

37
00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:53.258
Background means general information on a topic.

38
00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:55.072
Give some background.

39
00:01:55.683 --> 00:01:58.115
Your turn. Say: Background.

40
00:02:00.967 --> 00:02:02.270
Background.

41
00:02:03.017 --> 00:02:04.053
Revise.

42
00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:07.247
Revise means to improve a draft.

43
00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:09.037
Revise your essay.

44
00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:12.523
Your turn. Say: Revise.

45
00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:16.449
Revise.

46
00:02:17.233 --> 00:02:20.745
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:21.583 --> 00:02:23.943
Visal, how do I structure an essay?

48
00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:36.322
Use three parts. The introduction gives background and a thesis statement. The body has paragraphs that each develop one point. The conclusion restates the thesis.

49
00:02:37.417 --> 00:02:38.975
What is a thesis statement?

50
00:02:40.083 --> 00:02:49.780
It is one or two sentences that state your main argument, for example Online learning is effective because it is flexible and affordable.

51
00:02:50.883 --> 00:02:52.488
What should I do before writing?

52
00:02:53.583 --> 00:03:04.688
Analyse the question, brainstorm ideas and write an outline. After writing, revise your essay and check grammar, spelling and linkers.

53
00:03:05.833 --> 00:03:07.624
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:08.483 --> 00:03:12.364
Grammar focus: Thesis statements with because and although.

55
00:03:12.664 --> 00:03:13.816
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:14.517 --> 00:03:17.422
Online study is effective because it is flexible.

57
00:03:18.317 --> 00:03:21.326
Although it has risks, technology improves learning.

58
00:03:22.267 --> 00:03:28.205
A thesis statement makes a clear argument. Use because to give a reason and although to show a contrast.

59
00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:32.264
Be careful! Don't say: The thesis are in the end.

60
00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:36.838
Say: The thesis is in the introduction.

61
00:03:37.138 --> 00:03:38.708
Thesis is singular.

62
00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:42.199
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.082
Planning an Essay.

64
00:03:44.382 --> 00:03:47.183
Visal receives an essay question about online study.

65
00:03:48.167 --> 00:03:51.292
He analyses the question and writes an outline.

66
00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:55.437
His introduction gives background and a clear thesis.

67
00:03:56.433 --> 00:03:58.955
Each body paragraph develops one reason.

68
00:03:59.967 --> 00:04:02.941
His conclusion restates the thesis in new words.

69
00:04:04.033 --> 00:04:08.128
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:08.983 --> 00:04:10.762
The thesis is the main blank.

71
00:04:11.062 --> 00:04:14.507
A, title. B, page. C, argument.

72
00:04:18.067 --> 00:04:20.333
The answer is C: argument.

73
00:04:21.483 --> 00:04:23.227
The body has several blank.

74
00:04:23.527 --> 00:04:28.446
A, paragraphs. B, covers. C, maps.

75
00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.058
The answer is A: paragraphs.

76
00:04:35.217 --> 00:04:37.251
You write an outline blank writing.

77
00:04:37.551 --> 00:04:41.054
A, after. B, before. C, never.

78
00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:46.809
The answer is B: before.

79
00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:50.124
Revise means to blank a draft.

80
00:04:50.424 --> 00:04:53.508
A, lose. B, hide. C, improve.

81
00:04:57.067 --> 00:04:59.171
The answer is C: improve.

82
00:05:00.317 --> 00:05:02.165
What does the conclusion restate?

83
00:05:02.465 --> 00:05:06.281
A, the thesis. B, a joke. C, the date.

84
00:05:09.833 --> 00:05:12.065
The answer is A: the thesis.

85
00:05:13.267 --> 00:05:16.453
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:17.317 --> 00:05:18.921
How do you structure an essay?

87
00:05:27.717 --> 00:05:29.275
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:29.575 --> 00:05:43.236
An essay has an introduction, a body and a conclusion. The introduction gives background and a thesis. Each body paragraph develops one point and the conclusion restates the thesis.

89
00:05:43.536 --> 00:05:45.362
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:51.387
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and thesis statements with because and although.

91
00:05:51.687 --> 00:05:56.603
Today's value is strategic thinking. Think ahead, and choose your path with purpose.

92
00:05:56.903 --> 00:05:59.347
See you in Unit nine. Goodbye!

93
00:05:59.647 --> 00:06:02.740
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

